I see these posted periodically...is there an advantage to the Orcish
Wizard?

I ask because in my old *band days, a Half-Troll Priest was popular,
despite his low starting WIS and inability to get his WIS to the same
heights as a dwarf or human.  The huge CON and combat abilities made
the Half-Troll Priest a "warrior-priest", while a Dwarvish priest was
more of a "priest-warrior".

I'm curious if the Orc Wizard is the same idea...but I don't see a
whole lot of advantages.  You can eat poison corpses, which helps with
early Wizard hunger, but can't start with hungerless casting.  The pre-
Mines levels may be somewhat easier, but the Mines will be much
harder.  And you have the other pros/cons of a Chaotic.

Are there other non-intuitive combos?  The Gnomish Caveman
perhaps?  ;-)


